# Requests for checking a token, the data center host and the shape of a few responses by hand.
# Made for the REST Client extension in VS Code (humao.rest-client), the syntax works in similar tools.
# Copy .env.example to .env next to this file and put the host and the token there, .env stays out of git.
# A 300 with an empty body means the account lives in the other data center, change WRIKE_HOST.
@host = {{$dotenv WRIKE_HOST}}
@token = {{$dotenv WRIKE_TOKEN}}

### Who am I, the call the app uses to verify a token.
# @name me
GET https://{{host}}/api/v4/contacts?me=true
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Spaces the token can see.
# @name spaces
GET https://{{host}}/api/v4/spaces
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The folder tree.
# @name folders
GET https://{{host}}/api/v4/folders
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Workflows and their custom statuses.
# @name workflows
GET https://{{host}}/api/v4/workflows
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Tasks, one page of twenty.
# @name tasks
GET https://{{host}}/api/v4/tasks?pageSize=20
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Contacts, the reference data the app caches.
# @name contacts
GET https://{{host}}/api/v4/contacts
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
